{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Good Prospects", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "The Board Meeting", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 5, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 3, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Express duty, advice, willingness, or intention to do something in spoken or written texts and in work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "board", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the group of people who oversee the operations of a company", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Thank you very much, everybody, for attending today's board meeting.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le03ob05aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when you attend a board meeting.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to expedite", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to make things go faster", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We'll try to keep things brief in order to expedite the meeting today, Mr. Douglas.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le03ob05aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "amendment", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a change to an official document", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Are there any amendments to the minutes?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le03ob05aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "carried", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a majority of people have voted in favor of a proposition", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: All in favor of approving the meetings from March 25 of last year? Carried.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le03ob05aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "budgetary provisions", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the expected costs associated with a project", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I examined the budgetary provisions for that rental space.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le03ob05aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "all in favor", "type": "name"}, {"content": "what the chairperson of a meeting says to ask people to vote on a proposition", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: All in favor of the motion to change office space?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le03ob05aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "lawsuit", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the action of taking a person or company to court (using the legal system) to resolve a dispute", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Then, there is the problem of our unsettled lawsuits over plagiarism last year.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le03ob05aud09", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "market share", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the percentage of sales a company obtains in a specific area, compared to the total sales in that area", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We can count on our regular sales to the booksellers, but the school market share is still fragile.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le03ob05aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "call to order", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the official start of a meeting", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The BFP Publishing Board meeting is called to order at 7:00 p.m.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le03ob05aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn11le03ob05re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Result Clauses", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you want to talk about the results of something, you can use words or phrases like <span class=\"italic\">therefore, consequently </span>or <span class=\"italic\">as a result</span>. <br/>However, you can also use result clauses to make your writing and speaking more dynamic.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can introduce result clauses using: ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">so </span>and <span class=\"italic\">so ... that</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">So </span>comes at the beginning of the result clause.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">The three of us were very busy <span class=\"strong\">so we decided to hire more salespeople</span>.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You also use <span class=\"italic\">so </span>before adjectives and adverbs followed by a <span class=\"italic\">that</span>-clause (you can omit <span class=\"italic\">that</span>).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">The three of us were <span class=\"strong\">so busy (that) we decided to hire more salespeople.</span></span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "PFB has so many plans for growth that I feel the most pressing matter is the rental space.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Our operations budget shortfall is very large so I don't think we can afford it at the present time. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Our workbooks are so new that we don't have a significant volume of sales in financial literacy publications yet.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Purpose Clauses", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " When you want to explain the purpose or reason behind a decision or an action, you can use purpose clauses.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can introduce a purpose clause with:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">in order to ... </span>and <span class=\"italic\">so as to ...</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use these phrases to: <ul> <li>emphasize intention </li></ul> <br/> <span class=\"italic\">They arrived early <span class=\"strong\">in order to/so as to</span> prepare themselves.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ul> <li>express a negative purpose</li> </ul> <br/> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">In order not to be</span> late, I took a cab.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can also use<span class=\"strong\"> for </span>in front of nouns to express purpose.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "They did it <span class=\"strong\">for </span>the reward.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Thank you very much, everybody, for attending today's board meeting.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I recommend that we sign the lease for the spaces on the 10th and 11th floors in order to remain in the same building.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We could wait another six months so as to solidify our volume of sales before moving office space. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Go online. Find a short video of a meeting on a topic you are interested in. You can use the keywords \u201cmeeting on ______ \u201c", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Listen to the meeting. This will inspire you to write the minutes, but you can make up (invent) everything.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "In your minutes, include the following things: <ul> <li>The people in attendance  </li> <li>The time of the call to order</li>  <li>One motion (proposition)</li> <li>Arguments for and against the motion</li> <li>Motion carried or not carried</li>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Proofread your minutes for correct spelling and punctuation.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I listen to a video of a meeting.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write minutes for the meeting.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I give arguments for and against a proposal.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I say if the motion is carried or not carried.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"id": 0, "stimuli_ids": [0], "questions": [], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can discuss reasons for and results of an event or an action related to work and job.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can emphasize intentions or requirements related to job issues.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can present and respond to complex lines of argument in job situations.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " Do you enjoy attending formal meetings? Why or why not?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " What formal meetings have you attended? ", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " What was discussed at these meetings?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct", "allowed_attempts": 2, "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "Bring that issue to the board meeting!", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "img_path": "", "type": "WLC", "template_override": 1}, {"id": 1, "stimuli_ids": [1], "questions": [{"_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}]}